  "kind": "instance",
  "grade": "with:targets-list",
  "description": "The northbound target record is closed, and carries only what a surface needs to name a target and ask for a session on it. A serial record has no port at all: its options.port is a device path on the broker host, and a broker path never crosses C1 (V11; Contract §4). options, user, a credential reference and a login script are never in a record. host and port are present exactly when type is ssh or telnet, with the port in force. Consumers decode it strictly against this tag and ignore fields a later tag adds; a receiver treats an unknown type as opaque and shows it, never as an error (V5).",
  "corpus": [
    "Storage §3.1",
    "Storage §3.4",
    "Contract §4",
    "V11",
    "V5"
  ],
  "case": {
    "schema": "openapi/tsb.openapi.json#/components/schemas/TargetRecord",
